Notebook[{
Cell["Tracelet Basics", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"2362fb45-3ead-974f-a9fb-634a09ce4d19"],

Cell["\<\
WolframInstitute`HypergraphRewriting \[LongDash] derivations with the context \
taken away\
\>", "Subtitle",ExpressionUUID->"bb5eac1d-b0c6-ce4b-9d4b-2ac09b8a911e"],

Cell["\<\
After Nicolas Behr, Tracelets and Tracelet Analysis Of Compositional \
Rewriting Systems, ACT 2019, EPTCS 323, 44\[Dash]71 (arXiv:1904.12829). A \
tracelet is a derivation trace stripped of its context: the steps, and \
nothing of the hypergraph they ran in except what they actually used. Behr's \
characterisation theorem says every length-n trace is a tracelet applied to \
some ambient object, so the tracelet is what two traces have in common when \
they are the same derivation happening somewhere else.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b3058a92-6435-db49-b507-0ef99a239bba"],

Cell["\<\
In the categorical account all of this is pushouts and spans of monomorphisms \
over an adhesive category. Here it is tokens. The rewriting stack already \
gives every hyperedge an identity, with the event that made it and the events \
that used it, and that is the same data.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7cd6a5a9-a755-4442-a6d6-28bfe740607b"],

Cell["Loading", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"b9d795d9-69a8-d24d-b1dc-83ffc986b015"],

Cell["\<\
PacletDirectoryLoad[ParentDirectory[ParentDirectory[NotebookDirectory[]]]];
Needs[\"WolframInstitute`Hypergraphs`\"];
Get[FileNameJoin[{ParentDirectory[NotebookDirectory[]], \"RewritingSystems.wl\
\"}]];
Get[FileNameJoin[{ParentDirectory[NotebookDirectory[]], \"TraceletAnalysis.wl\
\"}]]\
\>", "Input",
 InitializationCell->
  True,ExpressionUUID->"53b8c31b-e2cf-c841-9f94-582d893e1491"],

Cell["1. Two ways for two steps to meet", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"2067c321-a780-7d40-bcb6-86ebd8361441"],

Cell["\<\
A system that subdivides an edge, started from a path of two:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"95219abc-19c6-1745-8f95-7ac5eb5fd150"],

Cell["\<\
sys = RewritingSystem[{{1, 2}} -> {{1, 3}, {3, 2}}, {{1, 2}, {2, 3}}];
HypergraphRulePlot[First @ sys[\"Rules\"], \"PanelSize\" -> 130]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"f5138d49-fb00-4c41-a01e-431e60ea8505"],

