Cell["\<\
And it really does: applying that one rule to the tracelet's input gives the \
tracelet's output, in one step instead of two.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a08854a7-98be-bf4c-98da-22dee98f4c56"],

Cell["\<\
CanonicalHypergraph @ First[HypergraphRuleApply[t1[\"Composite\"], t1[\"Input\
\"]]][\"Hypergraph\"] ===
  CanonicalHypergraph @ t1[\"Output\"]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"39bc6182-4b12-df4f-812c-21f4376dd24c"],

Cell[BoxData["True"], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"efc4a8e8-5d2b-3747-b9d6-3f81c6e2d213"],

Cell["\<\
The independent one composes too, into a rule that subdivides both edges of a \
path at once:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a939ba07-a5e2-fc43-b0c3-5e3c74906f47"],

Cell["HypergraphRulePlot[t2[\"Composite\"], \"PanelSize\" -> 150]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"5f9f785e-3417-af44-ae41-f39fc6c6b6de"],

