Cell["\<\
Counting the orders in which the steps could have been taken is Behr's shift \
equivalence, counted. One means the trace was forced; two means the two steps \
were independent and the order they came in was an accident of the run:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6e9bb155-e7d2-f94c-80d8-9fdfdfbec4c3"],

Cell["{t1[\"Linearisations\"], t2[\"Linearisations\"]}", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"97f8b8f2-2150-0f40-a4d8-0cbbd33ca64e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"1", ",", "2"}], "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"5c86df91-d990-5642-95bd-8d541479f99f"],

Cell["4. Where this meets the causal graph", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"e9989638-0bd3-e645-947b-3261cbe0500f"],

Cell["\<\
The causal order of a tracelet is the causal graph of the evolution, \
restricted to the steps of that trace and renumbered. The two are the same \
object seen from two distances: the causal graph says which of the events \
that happened depended on which, and the tracelet says what the dependence \
was made of and what the smallest hypergraph is in which it could happen at \
all.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"298a6f81-d970-b040-b101-7d0f23a5ec86"],

Cell["sys[2][\"CausalGraph\", ImageSize -> 560]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"2f6c0d00-edf9-d64e-b097-4b76df0d396e"],

